    "narrative": "For this May 20th slate, the heart of our lineup features two elite plays that anchor the Ghost Ride the WHIP offense. **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (75.27) are our premier options. **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a substantial +14% platoon boost and favorable park factors against Leiter, making him an absolute lock. Similarly, **Tyler Soderstrom** draws a high-upside matchup against Kochanowicz; with an opposing xERA of 5.20, **Tyler Soderstrom** is primed for a multi-hit day given the significant SP skill advantage. While **James Wood** (66.41) and **Josh Naylor** (66.06) provide high-floor production, **Mickey Moniak** and **Tyler Soderstrom** represent our most efficient paths to volume in the R, HR, and RBI categories today.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved choosing between the marginal outputs of **Seiya Suzuki** (52.60), **Kyle Karros** (52.58), and **Cole Young** (51.91). Ultimately, **Seiya Suzuki** barely nudged ahead despite a negative wind factor and a tougher matchup against Harrison, though his lower score relative to our starters keeps him on the periphery. We are closely monitoring the lineup statuses of **Dalton Rushing**, **Brice Turang**, **Henry Bolte**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Tyler Soderstrom**; should any of these players drop lower in the order than assumed, their scores\u2014particularly that of **Dalton Rushing**\u2014will necessitate a re-evaluation to avoid falling below the efficiency floor.\n\nWe remain cautious regarding our SB scarcity strategy, as **Zach McKinstry** (46.99) is currently our only primary speed threat active, though his value is diluted by a poor matchup against Bibee and a low spot in the order. With **Corbin Carroll**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Jose Caballero**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** all currently unavailable due to rest or injury, we are leaning heavily on our depth pieces. We continue to hold **Trevor Story**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Alex Freeland**, **Carson Williams**, and **Travis Bazzana** in reserve, waiting for their respective situational advantages to align with the daily projections. Efficiency is the priority today as we attempt to protect our remaining game caps.",
